</node>
<node id="&quot;S&amp;P&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"REGULATORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Another credit rating agency that evaluates the Borrower's creditworthiness and long-term debt ratings."&lt;SEP&gt;"S&amp;P is a global financial services company known for providing credit ratings that can impact the Borrower's financial conditions regarding Senior Debt."&lt;SEP&gt;"S&amp;P, or Standard &amp; Poor's, is a financial services company providing credit ratings that influence the perception of the Borrower's financial obligations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Standard &amp; Poor's Ratings Services, a division of The McGraw Hill Companies, Inc., which provides ratings and financial information on bonds and other securities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Standard &amp; Poor's, a credit rating agency that plays a role in determining the Applicable Spread based on the credit risk of the borrower."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7512db866e03064d07553d82c7e6d5c8e89534c374c8143ef109f8e93559313f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fee5390db4c81e6a3b72054fd834f99fdd4cb8d125b870b7c1cf7a322a93313f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7ad77acda1b68541d5e2bdb49d6cebee502795dfeefa164f0cd2f7a67daae17&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c78753b3331bcf7ddbb72049ab994b78870b8f45e13fad8256dcc68e5ac35055&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ebf25dd09fd0ed913393086258363a4d89fbba7e722941eac930ed8d6c51144</data>
  <data key="d3">DOC-d78f3a912cf6a0d022b78fa6955d54764af5f4e9ad6a1aef69147ba45f381b9c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GAAP&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"REGULATORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"GAAP (Generally Accepted Accounting Principles) refers to the standard framework of guidelines for financial accounting, which the Borrower must adhere to in presenting its financial information."&lt;SEP&gt;"Generally Accepted Accounting Principles, which provide the framework for financial accounting and reporting that is relevant to the Borrower's operations."&lt;SEP&gt;"generally accepted accounting principles in the United States of America, including accounting rules prescribed by the Governmental Accounting Standards Board."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fa0678d958db442fcb1252228bf16e5bad67dc5abb758474a551ca176e51e721&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb9b7fb2566d1ef23c654ca95d8c88a248b85df0bbe2d654b4c3f4f2e37a81d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d593bf0583582d4937727ed1d91d746a466f5010e2fe8b361ecb3d629c95c411</data>
  <data key="d3">DOC-d78f3a912cf6a0d022b78fa6955d54764af5f4e9ad6a1aef69147ba45f381b9c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LIBOR RATE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"BASE RATE BENCHMARK"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Reference interest rate used to determine the interest on the Advances for the borrower."&lt;SEP&gt;"the amount of interest which would have accrued on all Advances from the Date of Taxability to the date of the Final Determination if the interest rate during such period of calculation had been the sum of the LIBOR Rate for each such Interest Period for such Advance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8f2f1160e9faff6f277cb14cbdbac457679da678506fc659a1e6b446d495e99b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1153d2ce9781f421ef9f8a96cfad97b1d0733ca1ff10f84a402988b66edf1e41</data>
  <data key="d3">DOC-d78f3a912cf6a0d022b78fa6955d54764af5f4e9ad6a1aef69147ba45f381b9c</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AMENDMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"AMENDMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This term refers to formal changes, modifications, or additions to the existing credit agreement that may be necessary as circumstances evolve."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-27e959b2b2ebf635e7efa5c4d57ee3a43c19d2c3fe045f2cae758e858a15c58c</data>
